# A Guided Laboratory for Order Correspondences

A correspondence may offer many outputs, but an extension law keeps those outputs coherent as source objects grow. Begin with the [general idea of a preorder](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preorder), then inspect individual witness fibres below.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

The universal pullback accepts a source only when **every** related target passes. The next diagram displays acceptance and the first forbidden pattern.

{{visualization:0}}

<details><summary>Reveal the precise extension law</summary>

For preorders $A$ and $B$, a relation $R$ is an order correspondence when $a_0\le a_1$ and $R(a_0,b_0)$ imply the existence of $b_1\ge b_0$ with $R(a_1,b_1)$. Explore those witnesses interactively.

